# ---------- .NET build ----------
bin/
obj/
publish/
artifacts/
*.binlog

# ---------- Test & coverage output ----------
TestResults/
test-results/
playwright-report/
*.trx
coverage/
coverage*.json
coverage*.xml
coverage*.info
*.coverage

# ---------- IDE / personal state ----------
.vs/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
*.DotSettings.user
.vshistory/
.localhistory/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/tasks.json
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
# Note: Properties/launchSettings.json is committed ON PURPOSE - ports and
# profile names only, no secrets; it keeps "dotnet run" identical for everyone.

# ---------- Local database (SQLite) ----------
# *.db-* catches -shm, -wal AND -journal (rollback-journal pre-image pages
# are a copy of your data); *.sqlite* variants catch alternate naming.
*.db
*.db-*
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite-*

# ---------- Angular / Node ----------
node_modules/
dist/
.angular/
.eslintcache
*.tsbuildinfo
*.log
logs/
[Ll]og/
npm-debug.log*
# No private registry in this project; a root .npmrc is where auth tokens
# land if npm login is ever run - safer ignored. Re-track deliberately if
# shared registry config is ever needed.
.npmrc

# ---------- NuGet ----------
# Restored packages live in the global cache, not the repo. Only pack
# output needs ignoring; lock files and nuget.config stay committed.
*.nupkg
*.snupkg

# ---------- Config & secrets - never commit real values ----------
# Committed: appsettings.json (non-secret baseline) and
# appsettings.Development.json (SQLite path + log levels only).
# "appsettings.*.json" requires text between the dots, so it never matches
# appsettings.json itself.
appsettings.*.json
!appsettings.Development.json
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets.json
local.settings.json
# JetBrains/VS .http files are committed; their variable store (where
# tokens go) is not.
http-client.private.env.json

# ---------- Azure / cloud ----------
# az CLI + azd state: cached tokens, and azd environment folders whose
# .env files hold real resolved connection strings
.azure/
azureauth.json
# Database exports/backups are a full copy of your data
*.bacpac
*.dacpac
*.bak
azure-export/
# Deploy-time parameter files with real values; the Bicep/ARM templates
# themselves ARE committed (and are compiled by CI, never into the repo)
*.parameters.local.json
parameters.local.json
# Publish profiles + tooling droppings - endpoints, keys, deploy creds
*.pubxml
*.pubxml.user
PublishProfiles/
*.publishsettings
serviceDependencies.json
serviceDependencies.*.json
ApplicationInsights.config
# No zips belong in this repo; deploy zips from publish workflows land at
# the root, so take the broad rule intentionally
*.zip

# ---------- OS ----------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---------- AI assistant / editor-agent local state - never committed ----------
# Session state, permissions, and launch configs are personal tooling, not
# project code. Applies to the whole tree on every branch.
.claude/
.mcp.json
.cursor/
.aider*

# ---------- Additional credential hardening ----------
# Belt-and-braces beyond the config & secrets section above: common token/
# credential file shapes that should never exist in the tree at all.
# Note for the Angular side: there is no "frontend secrets file" pattern to
# protect, by design - anything compiled into browser code is public, so
# secrets must never enter lottery-web at all. .env*, .npmrc, and the rules
# below cover the files where tokens would otherwise land.
.netrc
_netrc
*.token
*.credentials
credentials.json
service-account*.json
*.keystore
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
*.asc
